{"highest":4,"ids":{"sre lens, medium: When _ccgl_race_note_post_v returns rc 1 (POST definitively failed), and then _ccgl_remove_label also fails, the zbuild:claimed label stays on the issue; no event names the stuck label — the pipeline.claim.skipped event that the engine eventually emits says only \"coordinator failed\", not that the label is still there and will block the next run. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"_ccgl_remove_label \"$issue\" \"$_CCGL_LABEL\" || true\"; happens when: A transient GitHub API outage hits both the note POST and the label-removal call in the same claim attempt; the first real API failure is expected, but the label that was successfully added moments before now has no cleanup path and no specific visibility.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: when _ccgl_remove_label fails in the backend_error cleanup paths, an event or a stderr line says the label may still be on the issue and the next run may be blocked — not only that the coordinator failed.); the same kind of problem also at: plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh | _ccgl_remove_label \"$issue\" \"$_CCGL_LABEL\" || true":"RLSRE-1","sre lens, low: The DSRACE-7 re-read of the issue after posting the holder record swallows its own failure with || true and no event or stderr line; if the re-read fails, arbitration continues with stale label state and no record of why. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"_ccgl_read_labels \"$issue\" || true\"; happens when: A momentary GitHub API error on the issue-view call that follows the note POST; the run proceeds to arbitration without any log entry that the re-read was skipped.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: a failure of _ccgl_read_labels in the DSRACE-7 re-read path produces at least a stderr line saying the re-read failed and arbitration is proceeding without fresh state.)":"RLSRE-2","sre lens, low: When the losing run's PATCH of its concurrent-claim note to \"not started\" fails, the failure is consumed by || true with no event or stderr line; an operator watching the issue sees the note body remain as \"concurrent claim by `<holder>`\" with no indication that the update was attempted and failed. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"_ccgl_race_note_update \"$note_id\" \"$_CCGL_SLUG\" \"$issue\" \"$winner\" || true\"; happens when: A transient PATCH failure after the race is settled; the loser has already been refused, so the failure is non-blocking, but the note stays in a misleading state and nothing says why.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: a failure of _ccgl_race_note_update produces at least a stderr line naming the note id and winner so an operator can tell whether the \"not started\" update was lost.)":"RLSRE-3","sre lens, medium: Four new lines pipe grep's output into head -1, which exits early once it reads one line; under set -euo pipefail, grep takes SIGPIPE when call-sequence has more entries than head reads, causing the pipeline to exit non-zero inside the subshell — the assignment gets an empty string and the ordering assertions silently pass or fail on a blank. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh: \"_post_line=\"$(/usr/bin/grep -n \"^POST_NOTE$\" \"$GHS/call-sequence\" | /usr/bin/head -1 | cut -d: -f1)\"\"; happens when: Any future test scenario that calls claim_coordinator_claim twice without resetting GHS (so POST_NOTE appears more than once in call-sequence), or a parallel test runner that appends to call-sequence concurrently.; fix: test; ACCEPTED IF: the four ordering-line extractions use a form that cannot receive SIGPIPE — grep directly against the file with a line-number, captured in full and trimmed in bash, or a here-string — rather than piping grep into head; and the sigpipe guard's | head scan, which now excludes -test.sh files, covers this test file or the test carries a sigpipe-ok annotation with a stated reason.); the same kind of problem also at: plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh | _get_line=\"$(/usr/bin/grep -n \"^GET_NOTES$\" \"$GHS/call-sequence\" | /usr/bin/head -1 | cut -d: -f1)\"; plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh | _post_line=\"$(/usr/bin/grep -n \"^POST_NOTE$\" \"$GHS/call-sequence\" | /usr/bin/head -1 | cut -d: -f1)\"; plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh | _get_line=\"$(/usr/bin/grep -n \"^GET_NOTES$\" \"$GHS/call-sequence\" | /usr/bin/head -1 | cut -d: -f1)\"":"RLSRE-4"}}
